\date{}
\begin{document}
\maketitle
\section{Introduction}
Maasina Fulfulde (Maasinankoore; ISO 639-3 ffm) is the most widely spoken Fula variety in Mali and has national-language status. One search found background and a lexicon but no Malian school textbooks or official curriculum documents.
\section{Primary Educational Resources}
No Malian school textbooks were found. A report mentions classroom materials and a children's alphabet book for Pulaar (a different Fula variety) in connection with the ADLaM script: \url{https://www.blackenterprise.com/barry-brothers-microsoft-and-mccann-pulaar-fulani/amp/}
\section{Linguistic and Reference Materials}
\begin{itemize}
\item Wikipedia, Maasina Fulfulde: \url{https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Maasina_Fulfulde}
\item Wikipedia, Fula alphabets (Latin alphabet standardised 1967, 32 letters; ADLaM): \url{https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fula_alphabets}
\item \textit{Fulfulde Maasina--English--French Lexicon}, Michigan State University Press: \url{https://msupress.org/9780870139420/fulfulde-maasina-english-french-lexicon}
\item Bibliography at MSU Matrix (Fulfulde-related): \url{https://alma.matrix.msu.edu/assets/uploads/2009/04/bibliographyfarysilateka.pdf}
\end{itemize}
\section{Religious and Community Resources}
None found in this search.
\section{Digital and Audio Resources}
\begin{itemize}
\item Fulfulde language learning resources, University of Wisconsin LCTL resource guide: \url{https://wisc.pb.unizin.org/lctlresources/chapter/fulfulde-language-learning-resources/}
\end{itemize}
\section{Curriculum Development Context}
Humery (2016), ``La litt\'eratie pulaar,'' discusses mother-tongue literacy programmes in the Senegal River valley (Senegal, not Mali), useful as a comparison: \url{https://journals.openedition.org/cres/2348}. Malian ministry materials for national-language instruction were not found and should be sought directly.
\end{document}
